{"name":"Sub-Zero","hex":"#57a1ce","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sub-zero","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["below 0°C; freezing cold","below 0°F (−18°C)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sub-zero"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sub-Zero (Mortal Kombat)","blocks":[{"text":"Sub-Zero is the name of two fictional characters in the Mortal Kombat fighting game franchise by Midway Games and NetherRealm Studios. Warriors from the fictional Lin Kuei clan, the two possess the ability to control ice in many forms. Characters by the name are the only fighters to appear in every main installment of the series, along with the action-adventure spin-off Mortal Kombat Mythologies: Sub-Zero (1997)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/79/Sub-Zero_John_Tobias_1996_Art.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-Zero_(Mortal_Kombat)"},{"title":"Characters of the Mortal Kombat series","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of playable and boss characters from the Mortal Kombat fighting game franchise and the games in which they appear. Created by Ed Boon and John Tobias, the series depicts conflicts between various realms. Most characters fight on behalf of their realm, with the primary heroes defending Earthrealm against conquering villains from Outworld and the Netherrealm. Early installments feature the characters participating in the eponymous Mortal Kombat tournament to decide their realm's fate. In later installments, Earthrealm is often invaded by force."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e4/MK_Armageddon_cast.png/330px-MK_Armageddon_cast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Characters_of_the_Mortal_Kombat_series"},{"title":"Sub-Zero (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Sub-Zero Group, Inc. is a privately held American company that manufactures and sells luxury kitchen appliances. It sells refrigerators and wine preservation products under the Sub-Zero brand. The company also manufactures kitchen appliances under the Wolf brand and dishwashers under the Cove brand name. Sub-Zero Group is based in Madison, Wisconsin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-Zero_(company)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Sub-Zero_prototype.png/250px-Sub-Zero_prototype.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Sub-Zero_prototype.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Sub-Zero_prototype.png/250px-Sub-Zero_prototype.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"John Tobias' original concept art and idea notes for the \"Lin Kuei / Ninja\" character that would become Sub-Zero.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASub-Zero_prototype.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sub-Zero_%28MK1%29.jpg/500px-Sub-Zero_%28MK1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sub-Zero_%28MK1%29.jpg/500px-Sub-Zero_%28MK1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sub-Zero in Mortal Kombat 1","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASub-Zero_(MK1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Joe_Taslim_at_the_2025_Toronto_International_Film_Festival.jpg/500px-Joe_Taslim_at_the_2025_Toronto_International_Film_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Joe_Taslim_at_the_2025_Toronto_International_Film_Festival.jpg/1280px-Joe_Taslim_at_the_2025_Toronto_International_Fil